  "notes": "Cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields, which report cause_code=TBD and category=provisional; narrative provides a detailed proximate cause statement (analysis inadequacy) but no official cause letter was assigned. Event identified via OE from North Anna LER 2021-002-00, modeled as a stub LER with SIMILAR_TO edge; plant/unit for the stub not specified beyond 'North Anna Power Station' in narrative. TDAFW pump and BDB AFW pump are referenced only as a corrective-action guidance context (pre-staging), not as a backup system operable during the inoperability window, so no BACKED_UP_BY edge was created — this event is a discovered unanalyzed condition, not a component failure with an active outage window, so no direct backup system applies to the Consequence node.  Two parallel FailureModes (loss of control power vs. hot shorts) both stem from the cable separation deficiency and both lead to the same Consequence, per rule 5."
